WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:02.656
- [Narrator] In the 1950s, wearing denim

00:00:02.656 --> 00:00:05.406
made you a rebel without a cause.

00:00:06.317 --> 00:00:08.520
And mainstream acceptance
lagged until one of the world's

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.437
most famous crooners
challenged the status quo.

00:00:14.137 --> 00:00:16.587
In 1951, American singer Bing Crosby

00:00:16.587 --> 00:00:19.719
tried to check into a
swanky Canadian hotel.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.155
Like many entertainers of the day,

00:00:21.155 --> 00:00:22.858
he was decked head to toe in denim

00:00:22.858 --> 00:00:24.718
so the hotel tried to turn him away.

00:00:24.718 --> 00:00:25.892
- [Man] You don't belong here.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.066
- [Narrator] Luckily, a
bellhop recognized him.

00:00:27.066 --> 00:00:28.281
- [Man] Hey that's Bing Crosby.

00:00:28.281 --> 00:00:30.156
- [Narrator] And the singer checked in.

00:00:30.156 --> 00:00:30.989
(ringing)

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:34.396
Word of this denim dilemma
in Canada got back to Levi's.

00:00:34.396 --> 00:00:35.845
- [Man] Uh-huh, uh-huh, done.

00:00:35.845 --> 00:00:36.678
(hangs up)

00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:38.913
- [Narrator] So the
company sprang into action.

00:00:38.913 --> 00:00:42.280
They developed a custom
denim jacket for Bing Crosby.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.631
It was decorated with
Levi's signature red tags

00:00:44.631 --> 00:00:47.896
and a large leather patch
labeling the denim as a tuxedo.

00:00:47.896 --> 00:00:48.979
(singing)

00:00:48.979 --> 00:00:51.547
Crosby rocked the new look,
and from that moment forward

00:00:51.547 --> 00:00:54.561
denim fashion was never the same again.

00:00:54.561 --> 00:00:57.061
(light music)

